 Used by an accounts-payable team to load supplier invoices into the ledger without retyping them.
 
-`extract_invoice(text, model)` takes the plain text of one invoice (from a PDF or an email) and a model, any callable that takes a prompt string and returns a string. The model reads the invoice and reports the supplier, invoice number, issue date, currency, the invoice lines and the total.
+`extract_invoice(text, model, date_order=None)` takes the plain text of one invoice (from a PDF or an email) and a model, any callable that takes a prompt string and returns a string. The model reads the invoice and reports the supplier, invoice number, issue date, currency, the invoice lines and the total.
 
-The function returns a dict with `supplier`, `invoice_number`, `issue_date` (a `date`), `currency` (three capital letters), `lines` (each with `description`, `quantity`, `unit_price` and the computed `amount`), `lines_total`, `total` and `status`. Amounts are `Decimal`, rounded to cents. `status` is `ok` when the lines add up to the total and `mismatch` when they don't; a mismatched invoice goes to a clerk instead of the ledger.
+The function returns a dict with `supplier`, `invoice_number`, `issue_date` (a `date`), `currency` (three capital letters), `lines` (each with `description`, `quantity`, `unit_price` and the computed `amount`), `lines_total`, `total` and `status`. Amounts are `Decimal`, rounded to cents. `status` is `ok` when the lines add up to the total and the date is certain, `mismatch` when the lines don't add up, and `ambiguous_date` when the date could be read two ways; any status other than `ok` goes to a clerk instead of the ledger.
+
+**Dates.** The model copies the issue date exactly as printed (`issue_date_text`, which must appear in the invoice) and the code reads it, so the model never converts a date. A date with a month name, an ISO date, a dotted date, or a numeric date with a part above 12 has one reading. A slashed or dashed date such as `05/08/2026` is read using the `date_order` argument (`"DMY"` for Brightwell, `"MDY"` for US suppliers); without it, `issue_date` is `None` and `issue_date_candidates` lists both readings. Pass `date_order` per supplier from the supplier master.
 
 If the model's answer can't be read, or a field is missing or malformed, the function raises `InvoiceError` with a message naming the field.
 
